.\" nulldc3.1: the manual page of nulldc3, the nullDC Dreamcast emulator

.TH "NULLDC3" "1" "October 2026" "nullDC 3.0.0" "User Commands"

.SH NAME

nulldc3 \- nullDC 3.0.0, the Sega Dreamcast emulator.

.SH SYNOPSIS

\fBnulldc3\fR [\fISWITCHES\fR]... [\fIGAME\fR]

.SH "DESCRIPTION"

\fBnulldc3\fR emulates the Sega Dreamcast. Its debugger serves the web UI Dreamcast DevTools at
http://127.0.0.1:55543/ while it runs.

.TP
\fIGAME\fR
A disc image (.gdi, .chd, .cdi, .cue, .iso, .lst), a program that runs under reios (.elf, .bin), or \fBnodisk\fR.
Without one the emulator starts at its menu.

.SH "SWITCHES"

Every switch is written with two dashes. A word that begins with a dash is always a switch: an unknown one, or one
written with one dash, is an error, and the emulator exits with status 2 without starting.

.TP
\fB--config\fR \fIsection\fR:\fIkey\fR=\fIvalue\fR [ \fB,\fR \fIsection\fR:\fIkey\fR=\fIvalue\fR ]...
Values of the configuration for this run; they are not written to emu.cfg. The comma between two of them is a word
of its own.

.TP
\fB--portable\fR \fIdir\fR
Keep the emulator's files in \fIdir\fR (made when it is missing) instead of the directory of the executable.

.TP
\fB--shared\fR
Keep them in the per-user directories \fB$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/nulldc3\fR (~/.config/nulldc3) and
\fB$XDG_DATA_HOME/nulldc3\fR (~/.local/share/nulldc3) instead, with the nulldc3 directories of
\fB$XDG_CONFIG_DIRS\fR and \fB$XDG_DATA_DIRS\fR read behind them. An emulator installed where it cannot write is
run with \fB--shared\fR.

.TP
\fB--help\fR
Print the usage text.

.TP
\fB--version\fR
Print the version of the emulator, \fBnullDC\fR \fIversion\fR, and exit.

.TP
\fB--\fR
Every word after it is a game, also one whose name begins with a dash.

.SH "EXAMPLES"

.TP
Start at the menu:
nulldc3

.TP
Start a disc image in full screen:
nulldc3 --config x11:fullscreen=1 /path/to/your/image.gdi

.TP
Keep the files in the per-user directories:
nulldc3 --shared /path/to/your/image.gdi

.SH "FILES"

Without \fB--portable\fR and \fB--shared\fR the files are in the directory of the executable (the directory of
the file a symbolic link to it points at). Started from an AppImage
(\fBnulldc3-\fIversion\fB-linux-\fIarch\fB.AppImage\fR), whose files are a read-only image, they are in the
directory that holds the AppImage file instead. The layout is the same in every directory:

.IP
emu.cfg, the configuration
.br
mappings/, the input mappings
.br
vmu_save_A1.bin, vmu_save_A2.bin, ..., the VMU images
.br
data/dc_boot.bin and data/dc_flash.bin, the BIOS and the flash of a Dreamcast (without them the emulator boots
with reios)
.br
data/dc_nvmem.bin, the flash as the emulator writes it back; data/<game>.state, the save states
.br
data/dumps/, what the debugging dumps of the renderers write
.LP

With \fB--shared\fR, emu.cfg and mappings/ are in the configuration directory and the rest in the data directory.
The directories of reicast (~/.reicast, ~/.config/reicast, ~/.local/share/reicast) are not read.

.SH "SEE ALSO"
\fBnulldc3-joyconfig\fR(1); README.md of the source tree.
